{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>In the year</b> — This is Darius the Persian, of whom our early Sages, of blessed memory, said that he was the son of Queen Esther. Rabbi Moses said: 'for [it should say] בחדש at the beginning of the month in every place.' If so, why did he write 'on the first day of the month'? Now Zerubbabel son of Rephayah was the brother of Shealtiel, of the sons of Jeconiah; and because his uncle Shealtiel was great, he called him his son after his name, like 'and she became to him for a son,' and similarly 'and these are the sons of Michal daughter of Saul' — for she had no child, only she raised them. And Jehozadak the father of Joshua was High Priest in the First House when it was burned, as it is written; therefore his son inherited his rank when Israel went out from the exile of Babylon. Therefore Ezra his uncle did not serve in the High Priesthood in the days of Joshua, also in the days of his son and grandson, as written in the book of Ezra."], :book :haggai, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The quotation beginning 'for בחדש...' is attributed to 'Rabbi Moses'; the syntax of the Hebrew is elliptical and has been rendered literally. The scriptural references are left implicit by Ibn Ezra and resolved silently following standard identification."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Haggai" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"] ["Ibn Ezra on Haggai -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:24.753035609Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}